.TH UNP 1.SH NAMEunp \- remove unprintable characters.SH SYNOPSIS\fBunp\fR[file].SH DESCRIPTION\fBunp\fRcopies a file, or the standard input, to the standard output without itsunprintable characters, and reports each one it removed on the erroroutput with a bell: the character's code and the line it was on..nf    unp messy > clean     1 found in line   1     2 found in line   1.fiLine ends pass through.  So do tabs, though each is reported, as code 9..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOcharcnt, tr